rom the BVS-II Study</article-title><source>Int J Behav Nutr Phys Act</source><year>2005</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>6</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15943862</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1479-5868-2-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pivarnik</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rivera</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of pregnancy on heart rate/oxygen consumption calibration curves</article-title><source>Med Sci Sports Exerc</source><year>2002</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>750</fpage><lpage>755</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11984290</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005768-200205001-01210</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yach</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuckler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Brownell</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiologic and economic consequences of the global epidemics of obesity and diabetes</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>62</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16397571</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nm0106-62</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Martorell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Country development and the association between parity and overweight</article-title><source>Int J Obes (Lond)</source><year>2007</year><volume>31</volume><fpage